, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JLLmE5e1Ui3rerAfiZWT8g", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_5xx"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 380925, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JLLmE5e1Ui3rerAfiZWT8g", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 385324, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). Because of that, `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` came out as `2.68` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even` (commit 08d3cd5986), I changed the import and the `quantize` call to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check that reference myself. The fix is based on what the test and the code's own docstring say. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014rFfqQwV9mx2ciZhnmpdKM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GEx77vtyNDcQJoZgnsh7cJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AmR7syBJpQ2eA577P1iZJF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "t