ency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). Because of that, `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` came out as `2.68` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even` (commit 08d3cd5986), I changed the import and the `quantize` call to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check that reference myself. The fix is based on what the test and the code's own docstring say. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}